Subject: [PATCH 115/116] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250: Add RPMh sleep stats

The always-on processor keeps counters for the SoC-wide low power
modes (AOSD, CXSD, DDR) and for each subsystem in its message RAM.
They are the only way to tell whether system suspend actually reaches
the deepest sleep state, or whether a resource is still voted on.

Describe the stats region as on SM8250. The downstream rpm-stats and
ddr-stats nodes read their offsets from 0xc3f0004 and 0xc3f001c,
inside the same 0x400 region at 0xc3f0000. With qcom_stats, a 20 s
s2idle suspend shows AOSD and CXSD entered for about 17-20 s.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg

Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
index f01ada362..d134806be 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
@@ -1831,6 +1831,11 @@ aoss_qmp: power-management@c300000 {
 			#clock-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		sram@c3f0000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,rpmh-stats";
+			reg = <0x0 0x0c3f0000 0x0 0x400>;
+		};
+
 		spmi_bus: spmi@c440000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,spmi-pmic-arb";
 			reg = <0x0 0x0c440000 0x0 0x0001100>,
